# Pastimes and animals, as chains (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7). One asks what the other does of an evening, or
# how their beasts are, and the other answers as they are (pastimes.own, animals.own: by trade, age, wealth, trait,
# quarter and region); or one tells their own, and the other reacts as they are (pastimes.react, animals.react). A
# wager is offered and taken or refused as each can afford (pastimes.wager), and remembered for a few days.
# Openers that test the speaker's own facts have cooldowns, so they don't crowd out the scenes.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Pastimes: asking

rule e2_r_pt_ask
when concept=talk.pastimes pair.band=acquaintances|friends|rivals
cooldown 1d
say What do you do with yourself of an evening? | Any pastimes, yourself? When the work's done? | What keeps you out of trouble, #address#? | How do you spend a Restday, then?
then other: pastimes.own

rule e2_r_pt_ask_close
when concept=talk.pastimes pair.band=friends|family|spouses
cooldown 1d
say Doing anything tonight, #pet#? | What are you up to after supper? | You look like you've had fun. What've you been at?
then other: pastimes.own

rule e2_r_pt_ask_pup
when concept=talk.pastimes other.stage=young self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 1d
say What are you playing, #address#? | And what game is it today? | Who's winning, little one?
then other: pastimes.own

rule e2_r_pt_ask_stranger
when concept=talk.pastimes pair.band=strangers
cooldown 2d
say Fine evening for it. Off anywhere? Dancing, cards? | Forgive me asking. Is there music anywhere tonight, do you know? | Do you play at all? Dice, cards? I'm after a game.
then other: pastimes.own

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Pastimes: answering, as they are (self answers)

rule e2_r_pt_own
when concept=pastimes.own
say Not much. Sit. Talk. Sleep. | A song, sometimes. A cup, more often. | Whatever's going. Dice, if there's dice. | I walk. Just walk. Clears the head. | #saying#. I mend things. I sleep.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_young
when concept=pastimes.own self.stage=young
say Hunter and hare! I'm the hunter! | Knucklebones. I'm the best on our street. Almost. | Hide-and-seek, but nobody's found me yet. Since this morning. | I'm making a fort. Out of everything.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_adolescent
when concept=pastimes.own self.stage=adolescent
say Nothing. Nothing you'd know about. | Wrestling on the green, when nobody's watching. | Practising my steps for the dance. Don't laugh. | Sitting on the wall. With the others. It's a thing.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_old
when concept=pastimes.own self.stage=old
say Draughts by the chapel, and a long nap after. | I sit, I watch, I remember. It fills a day. | I tell the young ones stories. They pretend to listen. | Pipe and a bench. That's my whole kingdom.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_rich
when concept=pastimes.own self.wealth=rich
say Cards, concerts, the occasional hunt. It's exhausting, honestly. | We keep musicians. Somebody has to. | Riding, mostly. And dinners. So many dinners.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_poor
when concept=pastimes.own self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Pastimes? I work, then I'm too #tired# to do anything else. | Singing's free. So's gossip. I do both. | Dice, when I've a penny. I haven't a penny.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e2_r_pt_own_heights
when concept=pastimes.own self.quarter=heights
say The Sound Hall on Restday. The strings are passable this season. | Whist. Endless whist. | Garden parties. You learn to smile through anything.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_sump
when concept=pastimes.own self.quarter=sump
say Dice behind the rope-walk. Don't tell the Watch. | Squeezebox and a cheap jug, down by the drain-mouth. | Ratting. Penny a tail and the sport's thrown in.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_scholar
when concept=pastimes.own self.job=scholar
say I read. And when my eyes give out, I read some more. | Riddles. I collect them. Nobody else wants them. | I'm writing down the old songs before the old forget them.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_priest
when concept=pastimes.own self.job=priest
say I sing. In chapel. Out of chapel. It's much the same. | A little gardening. The gods like a tidy bed. | Chess, with the healer. She cheats. I forgive her.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_smith
when concept=pastimes.own self.job=smith
say Wrestling. Nobody'll go against me anymore. | I make little iron birds. For the pups. Don't tell anyone. | Sleep. A smith's pastime is sleep.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_guard
when concept=pastimes.own self.role=guard
say Cards in the guardhouse. Don't tell the sergeant. | Archery at the butts. I'm the best shot on my watch. | Sleep. And breaking up other folk's fun.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_sailor
when concept=pastimes.own self.job=sailor|fisher
say Shanties. A ship's no ship without them. | Knots. I tie knots. Fancy ones. For fun. | Carving bone. Long voyages, you need something.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_innkeeper
when concept=pastimes.own self.job=innkeeper
say Watching other folk's pastimes, and charging for the ale. | Pastimes? I've not had an evening off since I was wed. | Listening. You hear everything, behind a bar.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e2_r_pt_own_farmer
when concept=pastimes.own self.job=farmer|herder
say A pipe on the gate at sundown, watching the beasts. | Ploughing matches. I won one once. | The harvest dance, once a year. That's my pastime.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_crafter
when concept=pastimes.own self.job=crafter|woodcutter
say Carving. You'd think I'd have had enough of wood. | Making pipes. Willow, mostly. Some of them play. | Whittling toys for the pups up the lane.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_cook
when concept=pastimes.own self.job=cook|baker
say Eating somebody else's cooking, for once. | Sweets. I make sweets for the pups on Restday. | Gossip at the oven. Best gossip in town comes through a kitchen.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_miner
when concept=pastimes.own self.job=miner
say Singing. Down the shaft the echo's grand. | Dice in the lamp-room. | Breathing. Air. Up top. That's my pastime.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_merry
when concept=pastimes.own self.humour=merry
say Making trouble and songs, in that order. | Jokes! I've a new one about a goose, want it? | Dancing, mostly on tables.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_dry
when concept=pastimes.own self.humour=dry
say Watching other folk enjoy themselves. Fascinating. | Counting the bricks in my wall. I'm up to four hundred. | Nothing, and I'm very good at it.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_humourless
when concept=pastimes.own self.humour=none
say I don't hold with pastimes. | Mending. Something always needs mending. | I sleep. That's what evenings are for.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e2_r_pt_own_quiet
when concept=pastimes.own self.talk=quiet
say ... Walking. | Needlework. | Fishing. Alone.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_chatty
when concept=pastimes.own self.talk=chatty
say Oh, everything! Singing, cards, I've a fiddle, I can't play it, but I've got it, and gossip, gods, the gossip... | Talking. You might've noticed. | Visiting! I visit. Everyone. Every evening.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_restless
when concept=pastimes.own self.drive=restless
say A bit of everything, and none of it long. | Walking out past the walls. Further every week. | Racing. Anything. Anyone.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_devout
when concept=pastimes.own self.piety=devout
say Hymns, and the chapel's flowers. | Reading the old prayers. | Helping at the dole. That's pastime enough.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_parent
when concept=pastimes.own self.parent=yes
say Pastimes? I've pups. Pups are my pastime. | Chasing the young ones home at dusk. | Mending what the pups break. All of it.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e2_r_pt_own_married
when concept=pastimes.own self.spouse
say Walking with #self.spouse#. Of an evening. | #self.spouse# and I play fox-and-geese. #self.spouse# wins. | Arguing with #self.spouse# about the fox-and-geese.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_frosthollow
when concept=pastimes.own here.region=frosthollow
say Sledging on the mine road. | Snowballs, when the shift's done. It's #very# #cold#, but it's fun. | Telling tales round the stove. It's a long winter.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_mirebridge
when concept=pastimes.own here.region=mirebridge
say Punting, when the river's kind. | Fen songs on the boards at dusk. | Eel-throwing. Don't ask.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_larkfield
when concept=pastimes.own here.region=larkfield
say Fiddling. Larkfield fiddlers are the best, you know. | Shearing races, in season. | Walking the downs. You can see half the realm from the top.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_southmeadow
when concept=pastimes.own here.region=southmeadow
say Cider in the orchard, a fiddle, the long evenings. | Dancing. We dance for everything down here. | Lying under the pear trees. Doing nothing at all.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_oakhaven
when concept=pastimes.own here.region=oakhaven
say Carving. Everyone carves in the Warmwood. | Tracking deer, just for the looking. | Climbing. Still. At my age.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_own_coldwater
when concept=pastimes.own here.region=coldwater
say Boats on Glasswater. Or skating, when it's ice. | Fishing the lake by lantern. | Swimming to the island and back.
then other: pastimes.react

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Pastimes: reacting (self reacts to what other said)

rule e2_r_pt_react
when concept=pastimes.react
say Sounds about right. | Fair enough. | #agree#. Each to their own. | Nothing wrong with that. | Can't fault it.

rule e2_r_pt_react_merry
when concept=pastimes.react self.humour=merry
say #surprise#! Then I'm coming with you, next time! | Ha! Now that's a life. | Count me in. I'll bring the noise.

rule e2_r_pt_react_dry
when concept=pastimes.react self.humour=dry
say Thrilling. | I'll try not to be jealous. | You'll want to pace yourself.

rule e2_r_pt_react_humourless
when concept=pastimes.react self.humour=none
say Hm. Waste of good daylight. | If you say so. | I've never seen the point.

rule e2_r_pt_react_warm
when concept=pastimes.react self.warmth=warm
say That sounds lovely. Truly. | You deserve it, #pet#. | Good. Everyone needs something that's theirs.

rule e2_r_pt_react_cold
when concept=pastimes.react self.warmth=cold
say Hm. | Right. | I see.

rule e2_r_pt_react_old
when concept=pastimes.react self.stage=old
say We did the same at your age. Just with more mud. | Enjoy it while your knees still bend. | My mother would've called that idling. I call it living.

rule e2_r_pt_react_young
when concept=pastimes.react self.stage=young
say Can I come? Can I? | That's boring. | Will you teach me?

rule e2_r_pt_react_rich
when concept=pastimes.react self.wealth=rich
say How charming. | Simple pleasures. I envy you, almost. | You must come to one of our evenings.

rule e2_r_pt_react_poor
when concept=pastimes.react self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Must be nice, having the time. | Wish I had the #money# for it. | Sounds grand. I'll hear about it from you.

rule e2_r_pt_react_restless
when concept=pastimes.react self.drive=restless
say I'd go mad in a week. | Is that all? | I've done that. Got bored.

rule e2_r_pt_react_devout
when concept=pastimes.react self.piety=devout
say As long as it's not on Restday. | The Bright One loves a glad heart. | Mind it doesn't keep you from chapel.

rule e2_r_pt_react_chatty
when concept=pastimes.react self.talk=chatty
say Oh, I love that! My cousin does that, well, did, until her paw, but that's another story. Do you know my cousin? | Tell me more. All of it. | Me too! Well, not me. But I could!

rule e2_r_pt_react_short
when concept=pastimes.react self.temper=short
say Pah. | Rather you than me. | Don't drag me into it.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Pastimes: telling, unasked (self tells; other reacts)

rule e2_r_pt_tell_song
when concept=talk.pastimes self.humour=merry
cooldown 2d
say Learned a new song. Want to hear it? Too late. | I danced till my tail fell off last night. | I've been practising a jig. Watch this. No, watch.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_tell_quiet_thing
when concept=talk.pastimes self.talk=quiet pair.band=friends|family|spouses
cooldown 2d
say I've finished the carving. The fox. If you want it. | I've been learning the pipes. Don't tell anyone. | Started a sampler. Your name's on it.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_tell_old
when concept=talk.pastimes self.stage=old
cooldown 2d
say Beat the miller's father at draughts. First time in a year. | I sang in chapel today. Voice held, mostly. | Told the pups the frost giant story. They screamed. Good.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_tell_pup
when concept=talk.pastimes self.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say I won at knucklebones! Five times! | I can do a cartwheel! Nearly! | We're playing hunter and hare and I'm the hare and I'm hiding. Shh.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_tell_rich
when concept=talk.pastimes self.wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say We've hired a harpist for the season. | Lost a fortune at whist last night. Well, a small fortune. | The House is hunting on the downs next week.
then other: pastimes.react

rule e2_r_pt_tell_scholar
when concept=talk.pastimes self.job=scholar
cooldown 2d
say I've found three hundred riddles in an old book. Three hundred! | I'm copying out a book of ballads. Every verse. | The almanac has a game in it. Nobody remembers the rules.
then other: pastimes.react

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Wagers

rule e2_r_pt_wager_offer
when concept=talk.pastimes pair.band=friends|acquaintances|rivals
cooldown 2d
say I'll wager you a penny I can beat you to the well. | Fancy #bet#? Two pennies says the baker's late tomorrow. | I'll bet you can't name every House in the realm. | A penny says it rains by dusk.
then other: pastimes.wager

rule e2_r_pt_wager_owed
when concept=talk.pastimes pair.mem.wager
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Don't think I've forgotten that wager. | About that #bet# of ours. | You still owe me, from the wager.
then other: pastimes.wager

rule e2_r_pt_wager_take
when concept=pastimes.wager
say Done. Shake on it. | You're on. | Fine. A penny. | Easy money.
remember pair: wager 3d

rule e2_r_pt_wager_rich
when concept=pastimes.wager self.wealth=rich
say A penny? Make it a crown, or what's the point? | Done. And I'll not take your penny if you lose. | Fine. I'll even give you a start.
remember pair: wager 3d

rule e2_r_pt_wager_poor
when concept=pastimes.wager self.wealth=poor
say A penny's bread, #address#. Make it a turnip. | I'll bet, but I'll not pay. | Half a penny. That's my limit.
remember pair: wager 3d

rule e2_r_pt_wager_destitute
when concept=pastimes.wager self.wealth=destitute
priority 1
say I've not a penny to my name. | Bet with what? My shadow? | If I had a penny I'd eat it.

rule e2_r_pt_wager_devout
when concept=pastimes.wager self.piety=devout
say No wagers. Not me. | The priest says gambling's the Dark One's door. | I'll pray for you to win. That's as far as I go.

rule e2_r_pt_wager_sly
when concept=pastimes.wager self.honesty=sly
say Done. But we'll do it my way. | Of course. Who's holding the money? Me? | Done. Mind, I never said which well.
remember pair: wager 3d

rule e2_r_pt_wager_frank
when concept=pastimes.wager self.honesty=frank
say No. I'd win, and you'd sulk. | I'll bet, but you'll lose. I'm telling you now. | All right. Fair and square.
remember pair: wager 3d

rule e2_r_pt_wager_humourless
when concept=pastimes.wager self.humour=none
say No. | I don't bet. | What for?

rule e2_r_pt_wager_merry
when concept=pastimes.wager self.humour=merry
say Done! And loser sings in the square. | Double it! | Done, and loser buys the cider.
remember pair: wager 3d

rule e2_r_pt_wager_owing
when concept=pastimes.wager self.owes=yes
priority 1
say I can't. I owe half the street already. | Put it on the slate. With the rest. | Don't. I'm in deep enough.

rule e2_r_pt_wager_remembered
when concept=pastimes.wager pair.mem.wager
priority 1
say What wager? | I'll pay. Tomorrow. Truly. | You cheated and you know it.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Animals: asking

rule e2_r_an_ask
when concept=talk.animals pair.band=acquaintances|friends|family
cooldown 1d
say Keeping any beasts these days? | How goes it with #beasts# at yours? | Got any creatures at yours? Hens? A cat? | Any trouble with the vermin this year?
then other: animals.own

rule e2_r_an_ask_farmer
when concept=talk.animals other.job=farmer|herder
cooldown 1d
say How's the stock? | And how goes it with #beasts#? | Lose any this winter?
then other: animals.own

rule e2_r_an_ask_pup
when concept=talk.animals other.stage=young self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 1d
say What are you looking at down there, #address#? | Seen any good beasts today? | Found another frog?
then other: animals.own

rule e2_r_an_ask_neighbour
when concept=talk.animals pair.neighbours=yes
cooldown 2d
say Was that your cockerel at midnight? | Your hens are in my yard again. | Have you seen our cat? She's been gone since Restday.
then other: animals.own

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Animals: answering, as they are

rule e2_r_an_own
when concept=animals.own
say Not a one. Mice don't count. | Two hens and a grudge against the fox. | Just the cat. Or the cat's got me. | Nothing. Never wanted the bother.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_farmer
when concept=animals.own self.job=farmer
say Cows are well. Hens are sulking. Pig's fat. | Lost a calf, but the rest are sound. | Fox had three hens. Otherwise, fair.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_herder
when concept=animals.own self.job=herder
say Flock's sound. Two lame. One stupid. Well, all stupid. | Lambs are coming thick and fast. | Lost a ewe to the cold. The rest are fat.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_fisher
when concept=animals.own self.job=fisher
say My stock's in the water, and it doesn't want to come out. | Fish are deep this month. | Seals have been at the nets. That's my animals.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_carter
when concept=animals.own self.job=carter
say My old mare. Knows the roads better than me. | Two horses. One's a saint. One's a demon. | The ox is well. The ox is always well.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_woodcutter
when concept=animals.own self.job=woodcutter
say I see more beasts than anyone. Deer, boar, a bear once. | Squirrels throw things at me. I'm not joking. | An owl lives in the woodshed. We've an understanding.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_miner
when concept=animals.own self.job=miner
say Pit ponies, and a canary to tell us when to run. | Rats down the shaft. Friendly ones. You learn their names. | I see nothing but rock. Rock's not a beast.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_cook
when concept=animals.own self.job=cook|baker
say The kitchen cat. Worth her weight in sausages. | Rats in the flour. Always the rats. | The geese for Restday. They know.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_innkeeper
when concept=animals.own self.job=innkeeper
say The inn cat's fatter than the guests. | Stabled six horses last night. One bit the boy. | A goose lives in the yard. It runs the place.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_sailor
when concept=animals.own self.job=sailor
say Ship's cat. She's been to more ports than me. | Rats. Every ship's got them. They're crew. | Gulls follow us home. Like a bad smell.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_guard
when concept=animals.own self.role=guard
say Strays. Goats, pigs, a cow once. All in my watch. | I've a horse, when the captain says. | That goose by the mill. My nemesis.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_priest
when concept=animals.own self.job=priest
say The chapel's bats. Gods' creatures. Still. | I bless the beasts at lambing. Most of them kick me. | A cat sits in the front pew every Restday.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_healer
when concept=animals.own self.job=healer
say Folk bring me their goats. I'm not a goat healer. I treat them anyway. | Leeches. Good ones. | Bees, for the honey. Honey heals.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_scholar
when concept=animals.own self.job=scholar
say I'm writing on the herons' habits. Fascinating birds. | A tame crow. It's cleverer than my students. | Beetles. In jars. Don't ask.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_young
when concept=animals.own self.stage=young
say I've got a beetle! In a box! His name's Hob! | I want a goat. Nobody'll let me have a goat. | I fed the ducks and one followed me home!
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_old
when concept=animals.own self.stage=old
say Had a cow once. Best friend I ever had. | Just the robin on the sill. It's enough. | Beasts? I've outlived three cats. The fourth's watching me.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_rich
when concept=animals.own self.wealth=rich
say Four horses, a peacock my wife insisted on, and the hunting stable. | The grey mare's from the south. Beautiful thing. | We've a gamekeeper for the beasts. I never see them.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_poor
when concept=animals.own self.wealth=poor|destitute
say A hen. When the fox lets me. | Rats. Do rats count? | Had a goat. Sold her for winter bread.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e2_r_an_own_heights
when concept=animals.own self.quarter=heights
say A songbird in a cage. It sings beautifully, if a bit sadly. | Carriage horses. Matched greys. | The cook keeps a cat. Downstairs.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_sump
when concept=animals.own self.quarter=sump
say Rats. Lots. We're on first-name terms. | A gull that steals from me every morning. | A three-legged cat that adopted me.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_larkfield
when concept=animals.own here.region=larkfield
say Sheep. In Larkfield, it's always sheep. | A dozen ewes and an old ram. Everyone's got sheep here. | Larks. The downs are full of larks.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_mirebridge
when concept=animals.own here.region=mirebridge
say Eels in the trap and frogs in the cellar. | Ducks. The fen's thick with them. | A heron stands on my roof. I've not asked why.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_frosthollow
when concept=animals.own here.region=frosthollow
say Pit ponies. And a goat that climbs better than me. | Reindeer, up the valley. My cousin herds them. | Snow hares in the garden. Eat the cabbages.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_southmeadow
when concept=animals.own here.region=southmeadow
say Bees. Southmeadow's all bees and orchards. | Pigs in the orchard, eating the windfalls. | A donkey that hates me. Loves my wife.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_oakhaven
when concept=animals.own here.region=oakhaven
say Pigs in the oak-woods, fat on acorns. | Deer in the garden. Bold as anything. | A squirrel that thinks it owns the roof.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_coldwater
when concept=animals.own here.region=coldwater
say Ducks on the lake. Swans, too, the bullies. | A boat, and the char beneath it. | A goat that swims. I'm not lying.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_own_ridgemere
when concept=animals.own here.region=ridgemere
say Gulls on the roof. Rats in the cellar. A proper city house. | The cat. The city's full of cats. | Pigeons. The landlord says they're mine. They're not.
then other: animals.react

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Animals: reacting

rule e2_r_an_react
when concept=animals.react
say #oath#. Beasts. | That's beasts for you. | There's always something, with beasts. | Sounds about right. | Mm. Same everywhere.

rule e2_r_an_react_nervy
when concept=animals.react self.temper=nervy
say #oath#! I'd be terrified. | Do they bite? | Keep them away from me.

rule e2_r_an_react_merry
when concept=animals.react self.humour=merry
say Ha! Bring it round, I'll teach it a trick. | I'd pay to see that. | I knew a goat like that. It ran for council.

rule e2_r_an_react_dry
when concept=animals.react self.humour=dry
say Lucky beasts. | And how do they feel about it? | Fascinating.

rule e2_r_an_react_warm
when concept=animals.react self.warmth=warm
say Aw, bless them. | Give them a scratch from me. | I love a beast that knows its own mind.

rule e2_r_an_react_farmer
when concept=animals.react self.job=farmer|herder
say Watch them in this weather. | Worming. Have you wormed them? | They're more trouble than folk know.

rule e2_r_an_react_cook
when concept=animals.react self.job=cook
say Bring it to me when it's done. I'll make it worth its life. | Sounds tasty. | Plump?

rule e2_r_an_react_old
when concept=animals.react self.stage=old
say Beasts are better company than most. | We had the same, when I was a pup. | Look after them. They look after you.

rule e2_r_an_react_young
when concept=animals.react self.stage=young
say Can I see it? Can I stroke it? | I want one! | Does it have a name?

rule e2_r_an_react_devout
when concept=animals.react self.piety=devout
say All creatures are the Bright One's. | Bless them. | The gods see every sparrow, they say.

rule e2_r_an_react_rich
when concept=animals.react self.wealth=rich
say How quaint. | I've a horse that cost more than your house. Not to boast. | I've never touched a hen.

rule e2_r_an_react_short
when concept=animals.react self.temper=short
say Keep them out of my garden, that's all. | Pests, the lot of them. | Don't bring them near me.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Animals: telling, unasked

rule e2_r_an_tell_farmer
when concept=talk.animals self.job=farmer
cooldown 2d
say The cow calved. Bull calf, all legs. | Fox got the cockerel. The hens are relieved. | #oath#, the new pig bit me. Twice.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_tell_herder
when concept=talk.animals self.job=herder
cooldown 2d
say Found a ewe on her back in a ditch, singing her head off. | The ram jumped the wall. Again. | Lost a lamb to the crows. Hate them.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_tell_fisher
when concept=talk.animals self.job=fisher
cooldown 2d
say #oath#, a pike as long as my leg took my lure and half my line. | Seals were laughing at me. | Heron took my bait and gave me a look.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_tell_young
when concept=talk.animals self.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say I saw a hedgehog! It was SO spiky! | There's a frog in the well! A big one! | A goose chased me and I ran SO fast!
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_tell_old
when concept=talk.animals self.stage=old
cooldown 2d
say Robin came to my paw today. Took the crumb right off. | The owl's back in the chapel tower. Like when I was a pup. | Saw the first swallow. I always look for it.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_tell_woodcutter
when concept=talk.animals self.job=woodcutter
cooldown 2d
say Bear in the far clearing. Turned and went. So did I. | Felled an oak and an owl flew out cursing me. | Boar ran right between my legs.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_tell_guard
when concept=talk.animals self.role=guard
cooldown 2d
say Chased a runaway pig the length of the street on my watch. | That goose has bitten me for the last time. | Arrested a drunk riding a cow.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_tell_carter
when concept=talk.animals self.job=carter
cooldown 2d
say The mare stopped dead on the bridge. Wouldn't budge. Then the bridge creaked. | Ox stepped on my foot. Took a while to notice. | Horse ate a whole sack of my apples.
then other: animals.react

rule e2_r_an_tell_hunt
when concept=talk.animals self.stage=adult pair.band=friends|family
cooldown 2d
say Ran down a hare at dawn. Felt like a pup again. | Saw a stag on the ridge, just stood there, watching me. | The boar are back by the stream. Big ones.
then other: animals.react

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Quips (one beat)

rule e2_r_an_quip_cat
when concept=talk.animals self.humour=dry
cooldown 2d
say A cat's a landlord who pays you in dead mice. | Geese. Proof the gods have a temper. | A sheep's thought is a lonely thing.

rule e2_r_an_quip_omen
when concept=talk.animals self.stage=old self.piety=devout
cooldown 2d
say Cows lying down. Rain by dark. Mark me. | A crow on the roof, three mornings. Someone's going. | The bees were quiet today. I don't like it.

rule e2_r_pt_quip_merry
when concept=talk.pastimes self.humour=merry self.talk=chatty
cooldown 2d
say If nobody's singing by dusk, I'm starting. | Life's short. Dance on the table. | The best pastime's the one that annoys the priest.
